const awaDetails = `<p>Enter a sacred space. Connect with yourself. Discover another way of seeing the world.</p><p>There are experiences you simply visit. And there are experiences that invite you to look within.</p><p>A visit to an <strong>Awá</strong>, the traditional spiritual guide and healer of the Bribri people, is one of the most profound experiences you can have while visiting the Caribbean of Costa Rica.</p><p>This is not a conventional tour. It is an intimate encounter with Bribri spirituality, held inside a sacred <strong>Usule</strong>, the traditional ceremonial house of the Awá.</p><h4>🌿 A SACRED SPACE</h4><p>The session begins by creating a safe and sacred space through <strong>traditional chants, meditation and spiritual connection</strong>. The Awá guides the experience according to the person and their intentions, creating a moment to slow down, reconnect with oneself and explore what may be happening within.</p><p>Different elements of nature may be incorporated, including <strong>fire, water, plants and air</strong>, according to traditional practice and the needs of the session.</p><h4>🌀 WHY DO PEOPLE VISIT AN AWÁ?</h4><p>Every person arrives with a different reason. Some seek:</p><ul><li>Spiritual cleansing</li><li>Balance and inner harmony</li><li>A deeper connection with themselves</li><li>Spiritual guidance</li><li>Understanding of their personal path or purpose</li><li>Support during moments of transition</li><li>A deeper connection with the spiritual world</li><li>A space for reflection and healing</li></ul><p>The Awá works from Bribri ancestral knowledge, helping restore balance and allowing life to flow with greater harmony.</p><h4>🛖 INSIDE THE USULE</h4><p>The Usule is more than a traditional house. It is a sacred space connected to the Bribri worldview and spirituality. The Awá may share aspects of <strong>Bribri cosmology and our way of understanding existence, nature, the spiritual world and the human being's place within it.</strong></p><h4>✨ AN EXPERIENCE THAT GOES DEEPER</h4><p>Sometimes we need a space to stop, breathe, listen and reconnect. If you feel called to experience something deeper than conventional tourism, this may be an opportunity to discover a different perspective on yourself, nature and life.</p><h4>⏱️ DURATION</h4><p><strong>Approximately 2 hours.</strong> The session may extend according to its natural flow.</p><h4>👤 GROUP SIZE</h4><p>For one person or a small group. <strong>There is no minimum number of participants.</strong></p><h4>💰 PRICE</h4><p><strong>From $120 USD per person.</strong> Private sessions may have a different rate. Contact us for the current rate according to group size and transportation needs.</p><h4>🚐 TRANSPORTATION</h4><p>Transportation from <strong>Puerto Viejo</strong> can be arranged as an additional service.</p><h4>🌿 WHAT TO BRING</h4><ul><li>Comfortable clothing</li><li>Water</li><li>An open mind</li><li>A willingness to connect, listen and experience</li></ul><p>There is no specific physical difficulty or minimum age. A nearby waterfall visit can be arranged separately.</p><p><strong>THIS IS MORE THAN A VISIT.</strong><br /><strong>It is an invitation to pause, connect and look within.</strong></p>`;
const cacaoDetails = `<p><strong>More than a tour - a journey into cacao, ancestral knowledge and the rainforest.</strong></p><p><strong>Approximately 5 hours · $95 USD per person · Easy · Minimum 2 people</strong></p><p>Step beyond conventional tourism and experience Bribri culture through <strong>cacao, plants, food, spirituality and the living rainforest</strong>. Hosted by local families, this experience invites you to participate, learn and connect rather than simply observe. There is no rush; every experience follows the natural rhythm of the people who join us.</p><h4>🌿 WHAT'S INCLUDED IN YOUR EXPERIENCE</h4><h4>🍫 Cacao Experience</h4><p>Discover the complete cacao process, from <strong>fermentation and drying to roasting and tasting</strong>, and learn about its spiritual connection to Indigenous peoples, the heart and human connection.</p><h4>🌱 Medicinal &amp; Ornamental Plants</h4><p>Interact with plants traditionally used by Bribri people and learn about their <strong>uses, benefits and cultural importance</strong>.</p><h4>🐸 Rainforest &amp; Wildlife</h4><p>Explore the forest, discover amphibians and wildlife, and learn about their place in the Bribri relationship with nature.</p><h4>🛖 Traditional Bribri House</h4><p>Enter a traditional house and explore the <strong>Bribri worldview, spirituality, dimensions of existence, human growth and purpose</strong>.</p><h4>🎨 Natural Painting</h4><p>Discover plants used to create natural pigments and, depending on the experience, create your own traditional-style painting.</p><h4>🍽️ Organic Community Lunch</h4><p>Enjoy a meal prepared with <strong>organic ingredients harvested within the community</strong>.</p><h4>💦 Waterfall Experience</h4><p>Finish at a beautiful waterfall where you can <strong>swim, relax and reconnect with nature</strong>. We also bring cacao to the waterfall for a natural exfoliation and a personal moment of connection with <strong>the earth, nature and yourself</strong>.</p><h4>🚐 TRANSPORTATION</h4><p>Round-trip transportation from <strong>Puerto Viejo</strong> is included.</p><h4>✨ MORE THAN A TOUR</h4><p>Meet people, learn from ancestral knowledge, connect with nature and discover another way of seeing the world. Meaningful cultural experiences begin with <strong>respect, curiosity and an open heart</strong>.</p><h4>🎒 WHAT TO BRING</h4><ul><li>Comfortable clothing</li><li>Closed-toe shoes</li><li>Insect repellent</li><li>Sunscreen</li><li>Water and snacks</li><li>Swimwear and towel</li></ul><h4>ℹ️ EXPERIENCE DETAILS</h4><p><strong>Duration:</strong> Approximately 5 hours<br /><strong>Price:</strong> $95 USD per person<br /><strong>Minimum booking:</strong> 2 people<br /><strong>Minimum age:</strong> No minimum age<br /><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy<br /><strong>Lunch:</strong> Organic community lunch included</p><h4>🛖 RESPECT FOR THE COMMUNITY</h4><p>This experience takes place within Bribri territory and is hosted with local families. To respect their privacy, culture and way of life, <strong>the exact meeting point and community location are shared only after the reservation has been confirmed.</strong></p><p><strong>COME WITH AN OPEN HEART.</strong><br /><strong>Learn. Participate. Connect.</strong><br /><strong>Experience Bribri culture beyond the surface.</strong></p>`;
const communityDetails = `<p><strong>A day of living, learning and connecting with Bribri culture.</strong></p><p><strong>Full-day experience · $111 USD per person · Minimum 2 people</strong></p><p>What if, instead of simply visiting an Indigenous community, you could be <strong>welcomed into a living culture and experience it through the people, the land and their ancestral knowledge?</strong> Spend a day within Bribri territory, welcomed by a local family and surrounded by rainforest. This is a hands-on experience where you participate, learn, taste and connect.</p><h4>🌿 A LIVING CONNECTION WITH THE FOREST</h4><p>Discover the relationship between the Bribri people and the rainforest. Learn how the community depends on the land for food, medicine and everyday life while caring for the natural environment. Visit a family farm and discover traditional ways of cultivating the land.</p><h4>🍫 DISCOVER THE WORLD OF CACAO</h4><p>Follow cacao through its transformation, from fruit to final product, and discover its importance to Bribri culture and knowledge passed through generations.</p><h4>🌱 MEDICINAL &amp; ORNAMENTAL PLANTS</h4><p>Walk through the natural surroundings and learn about plants used within Bribri culture, their traditional uses, benefits and importance.</p><h4>🏹 LEARN BY DOING</h4><ul><li>Practice traditional archery</li><li>Learn how Bribri houses are built</li><li>Explore a family farm</li><li>Discover traditional relationships with the forest</li><li>Experience the cacao process</li></ul><h4>🍽️ FOOD FROM THE LAND</h4><p>Enjoy an organic lunch prepared with ingredients <strong>harvested from the family farm</strong>. Food is another way to understand the relationship between the community and the land.</p><h4>💦 END YOUR DAY AT THE WATERFALL</h4><p>Finish at an easy-to-access rainforest waterfall for a refreshing swim, relaxation and peaceful connection with nature before returning to Puerto Viejo.</p><h4>🌙 TAKE THE EXPERIENCE FURTHER</h4><p>An <strong>optional overnight extension</strong> may include a traditional evening around the fire, a rainforest night walk, staying with a local family in a traditional home and additional cultural experiences. It is available at an additional cost; ask about availability when booking.</p><h4>🚐 TRANSPORTATION</h4><p>Round-trip transportation from <strong>Puerto Viejo</strong> is included. The exact meeting point and community location are provided <strong>after your reservation is confirmed</strong> to respect the privacy of families and the community.</p><h4>🎒 WHAT TO BRING</h4><ul><li>Comfortable clothing</li><li>Closed-toe shoes</li><li>Insect repellent</li><li>Sunscreen</li><li>Water and snacks</li><li>Swimwear and a towel</li></ul><h4>ℹ️ EXPERIENCE DETAILS</h4><p><strong>Duration:</strong> Full day<br /><strong>Price:</strong> $111 USD per person<br /><strong>Minimum booking:</strong> 2 people<br /><strong>Minimum age:</strong> No minimum age<br /><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy<br /><strong>Lunch:</strong> Organic lunch included</p><h4>🌿 A DIFFERENT KIND OF TOURISM</h4><p>This is about <strong>meeting people, learning from the land and experiencing Bribri culture through participation and connection.</strong> We ask guests to approach the community with respect, openness and curiosity. Exact locations and directions are shared only with confirmed guests.</p><p><strong>COME WITH CURIOSITY.<br />LEAVE WITH A CONNECTION.<br />Book your Bribri Community Immersion.</strong></p>`;
const riverDetails = `<p><strong>Travel by river. Learn by doing. Connect with Bribri culture.</strong></p><p><strong>Full-day experience · $225 USD per person · Minimum 2 participants</strong></p><p>The journey begins on the river. Travel deep into Bribri territory by boat and discover a place where rainforest, rivers, culture and community life are deeply connected. This is not a tour where you simply watch and listen. <strong>You learn by doing.</strong></p><h4>🛶 THE JOURNEY BEGINS ON THE RIVER</h4><p>Travel by boat through the rainforest and along the river toward the community. The boat ride is not simply transportation - <strong>it is the beginning of the adventure.</strong></p><h4>👩🏽 THE PEOPLE BEHIND THE COMMUNITY</h4><p>Discover the history of the community and learn about the women and local leaders who have helped create opportunities and strengthen community life. Hear their stories and discover the people behind the experience.</p><h4>🌿 LEARN BY DOING</h4><p>Participate rather than simply observe. You may explore medicinal and edible plants, learn about cacao, join cultural activities, explore traditional houses, discover local biodiversity and learn about the relationship between the forest and the community.</p><p><strong>The forest becomes your classroom.</strong></p><h4>🍫 CACAO &amp; ANCESTRAL KNOWLEDGE</h4><p>Discover cacao, its traditional uses and its importance within Bribri culture and Indigenous life.</p><h4>🌎 A TERRITORY CONNECTED TO TWO COUNTRIES</h4><p>Learn about the history and geography of the region and its relationship with the border between <strong>Costa Rica and Panama</strong>.</p><h4>🛖 TRADITIONAL HOUSES</h4><p>Discover traditional Bribri architecture and understand <strong>what these spaces represent</strong> within community life and culture.</p><h4>🍽️ A TRADITIONAL MEAL</h4><p>Enjoy a traditional lunch prepared within the community using local ingredients. Food is another way of connecting with the territory.</p><h4>💦 CONNECT WITH THE RIVER</h4><p>Enjoy time by the river to swim, relax and appreciate the rainforest after a day of learning and exploring.</p><h4>🌿 WHAT YOU'LL EXPERIENCE</h4><ul><li>Boat journey through the rainforest</li><li>Stories from community women and local leaders</li><li>Medicinal and edible plants</li><li>Cacao and ancestral knowledge</li><li>Traditional Bribri houses</li><li>Biodiversity and wildlife</li><li>Costa Rica-Panama border history</li><li>Hands-on cultural learning</li><li>Traditional lunch</li><li>Swimming and relaxing in the river</li><li>Round-trip transportation from Puerto Viejo</li></ul><h4>✨ MORE THAN A TOUR</h4><p>The most memorable experiences are the ones where <strong>you participate</strong>. Learn by doing, share moments with local people and discover the relationship between culture, forest and river.</p><h4>ℹ️ EXPERIENCE DETAILS</h4><p><strong>Duration:</strong> Full day<br /><strong>Price:</strong> $225 USD per person<br /><strong>Minimum booking:</strong> 2 participants<br /><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy to moderate<br /><strong>Minimum age:</strong> No minimum age<br /><strong>Transportation:</strong> Round trip from Puerto Viejo included<br /><strong>Boat journey:</strong> Included<br /><strong>Traditional lunch:</strong> Included</p><p><em>The itinerary may vary depending on weather, river conditions and community arrangements.</em></p><h4>🎒 WHAT TO BRING</h4><ul><li>Comfortable clothing</li><li>Closed-toe shoes</li><li>Insect repellent</li><li>Sunscreen</li><li>Water</li><li>Swimwear and towel</li><li>Waterproof bag for personal belongings</li></ul><h4>🛖 RESPECT THE COMMUNITY</h4><p>This experience is organized with local people and takes place within Bribri territory. We ask every visitor to approach the community with respect for its culture, traditions, homes and natural environment. Exact meeting points and logistics are provided after the reservation is confirmed.</p><p><strong>THE RIVER IS WAITING.<br />Travel deeper. Learn by doing. Experience Bribri culture from within.<br />BOOK YOUR RIVER &amp; CULTURAL EXPEDITION.</strong></p>`;
const jungleDetails = `<p><strong>3-Day Bribri Jungle Expedition</strong></p><p><strong>3 days · $600 USD per person · Minimum 2 participants · Challenging</strong></p><p><strong>THIS IS NOT A CONVENTIONAL TOUR.</strong> Leave the roads behind and enter the heart of the Talamanca rainforest. Jungle Immersion is a <strong>three-day expedition through the mountains, rivers and rainforest of Bribri territory</strong>, combining adventure, ancestral knowledge, wildlife, camping and cultural experiences.</p><p>For three days, we hike through the jungle, travel by boat, camp in nature, learn survival techniques, fish, forage, prepare our own food and learn from Bribri communities. <strong>The jungle becomes our classroom, our road and our home.</strong></p><h4>🌿 WHAT'S INCLUDED IN YOUR EXPEDITION</h4><h4>🥾 JUNGLE HIKING</h4><p>Explore dense rainforest and mountain terrain while learning to observe and understand the environment.</p><h4>🛶 RIVER &amp; BOAT TRAVEL</h4><p>Travel through the rivers and waterways of the territory by boat as required by the route.</p><h4>🏕️ JUNGLE CAMPING</h4><p>Spend nights surrounded by rainforest and experience the sounds and rhythms of the jungle after sunset.</p><h4>🔥 ANCESTRAL SURVIVAL SKILLS</h4><p>Learn traditional knowledge connected to living in the forest, identifying resources, navigating the environment and making use of what nature provides.</p><h4>🎣 FISHING &amp; FORAGING</h4><p>Learn traditional fishing techniques and discover responsible ways people have historically found food in the forest.</p><h4>🍳 COOKING IN NATURE</h4><p>Prepare meals in the rainforest using the cooking equipment provided by us.</p><h4>🐒 WILDLIFE &amp; RAINFOREST</h4><p>Learn about plants, animals, rivers and ecosystems and their role in the balance of the territory.</p><h4>🛖 BRIБRI CULTURE &amp; COMMUNITY</h4><p>Spend time within Bribri communities and learn about culture, traditions, ancestral knowledge and the relationship with the land. The rainforest is a <strong>living cultural landscape.</strong></p><h4>🌎 THREE DAYS OF CONNECTION</h4><p>Walk through the forest, travel its rivers, sleep within it, prepare food in it and learn from the people who have developed a deep relationship with this territory.</p><h4>💰 EXPEDITION PRICE</h4><p><strong>$600 USD per person · Minimum 2 participants</strong></p><h4>🎒 WHAT TO BRING</h4><p>Participants are responsible for personal camping equipment. A detailed packing list is provided before the expedition.</p><ul><li>Personal tent and camping equipment</li><li>Comfortable hiking clothes and closed hiking shoes</li><li>Insect repellent and sunscreen</li><li>Reusable water bottle and headlamp</li><li>Waterproof bags and personal toiletries</li><li>Extra dry clothes and personal medication</li><li>Small backpack suitable for several days outdoors</li></ul><p><strong>Cooking equipment is provided by us.</strong></p><h4>ℹ️ EXPEDITION DETAILS</h4><p><strong>Duration:</strong> 3 days<br /><strong>Price:</strong> $600 USD per person<br /><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Challenging<br /><strong>Camping:</strong> Included<br /><strong>Boat travel:</strong> Included<br /><strong>Meals:</strong> Included during the expedition<br /><strong>Personal camping equipment:</strong> Not included</p><p>The route may vary according to weather, river conditions, community arrangements and other natural circumstances.</p><h4>🌿 RESPECT THE TERRITORY</h4><p>The rainforest and rivers are unpredictable. Participants must follow the guide's instructions and respect the environment, wildlife, local communities and cultural spaces. Exact locations and routes are shared only with confirmed participants.</p><p><strong>MORE THAN AN ADVENTURE</strong><br />Three days. Jungle. Rivers. Mountains. Culture.<br /><strong>WALK THE JUNGLE. TRAVEL THE RIVERS. LIVE THE EXPERIENCE.</strong><br /><strong>BOOK YOUR 3-DAY JUNGLE IMMERSION.</strong></p>`;
const riverExperienceDetails = `<p><strong>Explore the rivers. Swim in the rainforest. Slow down and enjoy the journey.</strong></p><p><strong>Half-day experience · From $95 USD per person · Minimum 2 participants</strong></p><p>Sometimes the best adventures are the simplest ones. Travel by boat through the rivers of Bribri territory, surrounded by rainforest, wildlife and breathtaking landscapes. We travel at a relaxed pace, stopping to <strong>swim, explore, observe wildlife and enjoy fresh tropical fruit by the river.</strong></p><h4>🛶 THE RIVER IS THE ADVENTURE</h4><p>Travel through waterways that connect people, forests and different parts of the territory. <strong>Sometimes the river is the destination. Sometimes the journey is the destination.</strong></p><h4>🌿 EXPLORE &amp; CONNECT</h4><ul><li>Travel by boat through Bribri territory</li><li>Observe wildlife along the river</li><li>Explore rainforest landscapes</li><li>Stop for a swim</li><li>Enjoy fresh tropical fruit</li><li>Discover natural scenery</li><li>Learn about the relationship between rivers, forest and community</li></ul><h4>💦 TIME TO SLOW DOWN</h4><p>Swim in the river, sit under the rainforest canopy, eat fresh fruit and enjoy the surroundings. <strong>No rushing. No crowded itinerary. Just river, forest and connection.</strong></p><h4>🌿 ADD IT TO YOUR JOURNEY</h4><p>This experience can be combined with other cultural or nature experiences. Ask us about adding water, relaxation and adventure to your day.</p><h4>ℹ️ EXPERIENCE DETAILS</h4><p><strong>Duration:</strong> Approximately 4-5 hours<br /><strong>Price:</strong> From $95 USD per person<br /><strong>Minimum booking:</strong> 2 participants<br /><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy<br /><strong>Minimum age:</strong> No minimum age<br /><strong>Boat:</strong> Included<br /><strong>Fresh fruit:</strong> Included<br /><strong>Transportation:</strong> Available from Puerto Viejo</p><p><em>The exact route and river selected depend on weather, water conditions, safety and community arrangements.</em></p><h4>🎒 WHAT TO BRING</h4><ul><li>Comfortable clothing</li><li>Swimwear and towel</li><li>Sunscreen and insect repellent</li><li>Water</li><li>Waterproof bag for personal belongings</li><li>Comfortable shoes</li></ul><h4>🛖 RESPECT THE TERRITORY</h4><p>This experience takes place within Bribri territory. We ask every visitor to respect the river, wildlife, local communities and natural environment. Exact meeting points and route details are provided after reservation.</p><p><strong>LET THE RIVER TAKE YOU SOMEWHERE DIFFERENT.</strong><br /><strong>Travel by water. Swim. Explore. Connect.<br />ASK ABOUT THE BRIБRI RIVER EXPERIENCE.</strong></p>`;
const farmTableDetails = `<p><strong>Harvest. Cook. Share. Experience food through Bribri culture.</strong></p><p><strong>Approximately 4 hours · $95 USD per person · Easy · Minimum 2 participants</strong></p><p>Forget the typical cooking class. Before we prepare the food, <strong>we go to the farm to find it.</strong> Visit a family farm, learn about traditional crops, harvest ingredients and help prepare a meal using fresh products from the land. You do not just watch - <strong>you participate.</strong></p><h4>🌱 FROM THE FARM TO YOUR PLATE</h4><h4>🌿 Visit the Farm</h4><p>Walk through a family farm, discover everyday crops and learn how families cultivate the land and why agriculture remains important to community life.</p><h4>🧺 Harvest Your Ingredients</h4><p>Help collect ingredients that will become part of your meal. What we harvest depends on the season and what is naturally available.</p><h4>🍳 Cook Together</h4><p>Bring the ingredients into the kitchen and help prepare a traditional Bribri-inspired meal with guidance from our hosts.</p><h4>🍽️ Share the Meal</h4><p>Enjoy the meal you helped create. Food is more than nourishment - <strong>it is connection, community and sharing.</strong></p><h4>🌿 WHAT YOU'LL EXPERIENCE</h4><ul><li>Visit a family farm</li><li>Learn about traditional crops and cultivation</li><li>Harvest fresh ingredients</li><li>Participate in food preparation</li><li>Learn traditional cooking techniques</li><li>Prepare and enjoy a fresh local meal</li><li>Connect with local people and Bribri culture</li></ul><h4>✨ MORE THAN A COOKING CLASS</h4><p>From the soil to the table, every ingredient has a story. This experience can be combined with cultural activities or an overnight stay, depending on itinerary and availability.</p><h4>ℹ️ EXPERIENCE DETAILS</h4><p><strong>Duration:</strong> Approximately 4 hours<br /><strong>Price:</strong> $95 USD per person<br /><strong>Minimum booking:</strong> 2 participants<br /><strong>Minimum age:</strong> No minimum age<br /><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy<br /><strong>Transportation:</strong> Available from Puerto Viejo</p><p><em>Ingredients and activities may vary depending on the season and what is naturally available at the farm.</em></p><h4>🎒 WHAT TO BRING</h4><ul><li>Comfortable clothing</li><li>Closed-toe shoes</li><li>Insect repellent</li><li>Sunscreen</li><li>Water</li><li>A good appetite</li></ul><h4>🛖 RESPECT THE COMMUNITY</h4><p>This experience takes place within Bribri territory and in collaboration with local families. The exact location and meeting point are provided after the reservation is confirmed.</p><p><strong>COME HUNGRY.<br />HARVEST WITH US. COOK WITH US. SHARE THE EXPERIENCE.<br />BOOK YOUR FARM-TO-TABLE EXPERIENCE.</strong></p>`;
