const cahuitaDetails = `<p><strong>RAINFOREST &amp; WILDLIFE</strong></p><p><strong>Walk into the rainforest. Let the Caribbean reveal itself.</strong></p><p>Explore the trails of Cahuita National Park and discover the incredible life hidden within the forest. Look for monkeys, sloths, birds, reptiles, insects and tropical plants while walking through one of Costa Rica's most beautiful Caribbean landscapes.</p><p>This is more than a walk. It is an opportunity to slow down, observe and understand the forest.</p><h4>👀 WHY WALK WITH A GUIDE?</h4><p><strong>The rainforest is full of life - but not everything is easy to see.</strong> A trained local guide knows where to look, what sounds to listen for and how to move through the forest without disturbing wildlife.</p><p>Instead of simply walking the trail, learn to notice the small details: movement in the trees, a hidden reptile, a bird call, an unusual plant or the signs animals leave behind. <strong>The difference is not just seeing more. It is understanding what you are seeing.</strong></p><h4>WHAT'S INCLUDED</h4><ul><li>Guided rainforest walk</li><li>Flora and fauna observation</li><li>Wildlife spotting</li><li>Round-trip transportation</li><li>Fresh tropical fruit</li></ul><p><strong>Duration:</strong> 2 hours<br /><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy<br /><strong>Minimum:</strong> 2 people<br /><strong>Price:</strong> $75 USD per person</p><h4>🌊 WANT MORE?</h4><p>Combine your rainforest experience with <strong>Caribbean Reef Snorkeling</strong> and discover the Caribbean from two completely different perspectives.</p><p><strong>Full experience: $87 USD per person<br />One forest. One ocean. Two worlds to discover.</strong></p>`;
